# Free API key from https://finnhub.io/register (no card required).
# Powers live prices for every stock/ETF in src/data/stocks.ts.
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key, then restart `npm run dev`.
# Bitcoin's live price needs no key (CoinGecko, public endpoint).
VITE_FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Supabase project (auth + saved portfolios + the Nasdaq/NYSE catalogue
# backend below). Free at https://supabase.com. Find these under Project
# Settings -> API. The anon key is safe to expose client-side — it's the
# public key, protected by Row Level Security (see supabase/schema.sql).
# Leave both blank to run in local-only mode (no login screen, no catalogue
# search, everything saved to this browser instead).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nasdaq/NYSE catalogue backend — SERVER-SIDE secrets, never put these here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The full stock catalogue (supabase/functions/) runs as Supabase Edge
# Functions, not in this client app, so its secrets are never read from
# this file or any VITE_-prefixed variable (those get bundled into the
# browser JS). Set them instead in your Supabase project's dashboard, under
# Edge Functions -> Manage secrets — see README's "Nasdaq & NYSE catalogue"
# section for full setup steps.
#
#   MASSIVE_API_KEY            Your Massive (formerly Polygon.io) API key.
#                               Without it, catalogue-sync/quotes/bars/
#                               instrument-details/logo-proxy all return an
#                               honest "unavailable" response — never a
#                               fabricated price or logo.
#   MASSIVE_QUOTE_DELAY_SECONDS Seconds of quote delay your Massive plan is
#                               actually entitled to (0 = real-time-entitled).
#                               Operator-set — never inferred from the API
#                               response, since Massive doesn't self-report
#                               plan tier. Drives whether a quote is honestly
#                               labeled "real-time" vs "delayed".
#   CATALOGUE_SYNC_SECRET       A random string you choose. Required in the
#                               `x-sync-secret` header to trigger
#                               catalogue-sync, so a full Nasdaq+NYSE
#                               re-import can't be kicked off by anyone who
#                               finds the function's public URL.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   Auto-injected into every Edge Function by
#                               Supabase — you never set this yourself. It
#                               bypasses Row Level Security, which is why
#                               the catalogue write path only ever runs
#                               server-side, never in this client app.
